# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile copies: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
# rust-toolchain.toml and crates/. An allowlist, because a denylist misses what a run
# leaves behind: Docker anchors patterns at the context root, so `.nf-test/` does not match
# pipeline/.nf-test/, and a run launched at the repo root writes work/ (GBs, tens of GBs for
# --chrom all), .nextflow*, logs/ and results/ beside data/ and target/.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
